; casterload.eval - what inspectroute.eval's Caster saves come back as (code-review
; C99). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 23, which runs it as a NEW process
; on the same scratch world: the level and the kinds load from the files the
; saves wrote, so a caster written without its spell warns in this run's log
; (the skel_coward kind as it is built, the skeleton at 12,6 as it spawns).
; The judge demands no such warning, and both dialogs OPENING on the spell saved
; - not only showing it, since Open gives a spell-less caster's working copy the
; first spell offered, the same one the saves wrote. casterdefault.eval, run
; next with the spells taken out of the files, is the control for both.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
editor inspect 12 6
editor inspector
editor inspector esc
monsterdialog skel_coward
monsterdialog off
